35,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,The reviews show that shared spaces are rated much higher than isolated ones.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,The timetable data is alarming; we lost forty hours of teaching time to construction noise.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The diaries confirm six weeks lost to weather, and the rooms were out of service for two terms.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The tender records show plant costs have jumped twenty percent, but the reviews say shared spaces are loved.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The technicians have spare hours, but the manual routines are eating them up. We can shift that load.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, if the shared spaces are rated well, we should prioritize a plan that opens up the older blocks.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, but the booking data shows specialist rooms are barely used. We are paying for empty space.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, the specialist rooms are empty because the staff are too busy with manual routines to book them.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, if we can free up the technicians, we can afford the higher plant costs without breaking the budget.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Benjamin, exactly. The manual routines are the bottleneck. If we automate the checks, the staff can handle the new plan.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,The survey findings in the older blocks are worrying. Hazardous material behind partitions means delays.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,The booking data confirms the specialist rooms are underutilized. We should not build more of them.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,The decade of delivery schedules shows that projects with clear rationale finish on time. The others slip.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,The renewal reserve for equipment bought earlier is empty. We have no buffer for the price jumps.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"The technicians are the key. If we automate the manual routines, we can handle the new plan without hiring.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,We need a plan that opens up the older blocks but avoids the hazardous material delays.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. We should focus on general-purpose rooms, not specialist ones. The data is clear.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,The delivery schedules show that clear rationale is the only way to avoid slippage. We need a plan with a clear rationale.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"The price jumps are real, but the shared spaces are worth it. We need a plan that balances cost and utility.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,The technicians can handle the new plan if we automate the manual routines. That is the only way to make it work.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
